WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.544
[♪ upbeat music plays]

00:30.322 --> 00:33.951
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

00:44.044 --> 00:46.797
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION
SOME SCENES WERE GENERATED USING AI

00:46.880 --> 00:48.966
CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
WERE FILMED SAFELY

00:49.049 --> 00:50.259
[♪ marching music plays]

00:50.342 --> 00:53.136
THE CRADLE OF ELITE SOLDIERS

00:57.599 --> 00:59.518
-Company, attention!
-[soldiers] Attention!

01:00.727 --> 01:04.481
[officer 1] I don't care what kind of
people you were outside.

01:05.274 --> 01:09.403
The only thing I'm interested in
is making true soldiers out of you,

01:09.987 --> 01:12.823
so make sure to give it your all
in training. Understood?

01:12.906 --> 01:14.366
[soldiers] Understood, sir!

01:14.449 --> 01:16.535
That was pathetic!
Everyone, down on the ground!

01:17.286 --> 01:19.079
[soldiers] Down on the ground!

01:20.872 --> 01:23.875
[officer 1] On one, "I will."
On two, "Chant louder."

01:23.959 --> 01:25.836
-One!
-[soldiers] I will!

01:25.919 --> 01:26.920
-[officer 1] Two!
-Chant louder!

01:27.004 --> 01:28.589
[officer 1] Is that the best you can do?

01:28.672 --> 01:30.382
-One!
-[soldiers] I will!

01:30.465 --> 01:32.050
-Two!
-Chant louder!

01:32.134 --> 01:33.343
-One!
-I will!

01:33.427 --> 01:34.803
-Two!
-Chant louder!

01:34.886 --> 01:36.430
-One!
-I will!

01:36.513 --> 01:40.183
[narrator] Korean men have a duty
to serve in the military.

01:40.267 --> 01:41.268
[soldiers] Chant louder!

01:48.191 --> 01:50.527
[officer 2] What do you think
you're doing, putting on makeup?

01:50.610 --> 01:51.987
All troops, on your feet!

01:53.572 --> 01:55.490
To the signpost and back!

01:55.574 --> 01:56.992
Run!

01:58.702 --> 02:00.162
[officer 3] Faster!

02:01.038 --> 02:02.831
[narrator] Our Creed.

02:04.082 --> 02:06.543
One. We defend liberal democracy

02:06.626 --> 02:08.045
and help reunify the nation.

02:12.758 --> 02:18.221
Two. We train as if in real combat
and become victors in ground warfare.

02:18.305 --> 02:19.306
[soldiers] One!

02:20.307 --> 02:21.308
Two!

02:21.808 --> 02:23.435
-[soldiers] Three!
-[grunts]

02:23.518 --> 02:24.686
[soldiers] Four!

02:25.354 --> 02:27.189
[groans] What the heck?

02:28.899 --> 02:30.609
Sir, it's a rock!

02:30.692 --> 02:33.028
No kidding, you idiot.
Of course it's a rock.

02:33.111 --> 02:36.031
-I think I sprained my back. Help!
-[soldier 1] Come on, be quiet.

02:36.114 --> 02:37.741
-Help!
-[soldier 2] Hey, man. Be quiet!

02:37.824 --> 02:38.825
-Why am I!
-[officer 3] Two!

02:38.909 --> 02:39.910
Like this?

02:39.993 --> 02:41.495
-[officer 3] One!
-Why am I!

02:41.578 --> 02:42.996
-Two!
-Like this?

02:43.080 --> 02:44.456
-[officer 3] One!
-Why am I!

02:44.539 --> 02:46.083
-[officer 3] Two!
-Like this?

02:46.166 --> 02:48.335
-[officer 3] We!
-Can do it!

02:48.418 --> 02:50.420
-We!
-Can do it!

02:50.504 --> 02:51.922
-Left foot!
-[person 1] Three.

02:52.631 --> 02:54.549
-[officer 3] Left foot!
-[narrator] We obey regulations…

02:54.633 --> 02:56.093
[officer 3] Thirty seconds left to eat!

02:56.176 --> 02:57.928
…and follow the orders of our superiors.

02:58.011 --> 03:00.097
[officer 3] Anyone leaving leftovers
will regret it. Got it?

03:00.180 --> 03:01.264
[soldiers] Yes, sir!

03:07.187 --> 03:09.523
I can… [groans, panting]

03:11.024 --> 03:12.275
…do it!

03:12.859 --> 03:15.779
I can… [strains]

03:18.907 --> 03:19.908
Sir!

03:20.742 --> 03:22.869
Please… help me!

03:22.953 --> 03:25.622
It'll take more than that
to save our nation!

03:27.958 --> 03:29.543
[panting]

03:31.711 --> 03:34.923
[narrator] I can't save it because…

03:36.466 --> 03:37.801
I'm not a soldier.

03:38.593 --> 03:41.096
[♪ marching music plays]

03:41.179 --> 03:43.056
ASSISTANT INSTRUCTOR

03:43.140 --> 03:46.768
CONFIDENCE WALL
INCLINED WALL SCALING

03:53.150 --> 03:54.234
Oh.

03:54.317 --> 03:56.027
-[both grunting]
-[soldiers exclaim]

03:56.111 --> 03:57.821
-[bone snaps]
-[soldiers gasp]

03:57.904 --> 04:00.782
-Hey! Don't we have a medic here?
-[assistant instructor groaning]

04:03.285 --> 04:04.411
[assistant 1] Move!

04:04.995 --> 04:06.121
Hey, push!

04:07.205 --> 04:08.957
Wait! You shouldn't move him like that.

04:09.040 --> 04:10.834
[assistant instructor groaning]
STYLE
::cue()

04:14.588 --> 04:17.048
[breathes heavily] It's a fracture.
Any orthopedic surgeons?

04:17.132 --> 04:18.758
[stutters] I'm an orthopedic surgeon.

04:20.427 --> 04:21.720
-Please take a look.
-Okay.

04:21.803 --> 04:24.556
[orthopedic surgeon]
Sir, I'm going to apply pressure here.

04:24.639 --> 04:27.100
-Can you feel anything?
-How's the patient?

04:27.184 --> 04:29.770
[soldier 1] No fractures,
but the laceration is deep.

04:29.853 --> 04:32.439
We need to irrigate and suture it
before it gets infected.

04:33.815 --> 04:35.901
Do we have any alcohol
and saline solution?

04:40.489 --> 04:42.616
Don't scrunch your face,
or the wound might open.

04:42.699 --> 04:43.700
Please hang in there.

04:43.784 --> 04:45.744
Hand me the saline solution. Hurry.

04:45.827 --> 04:47.621
Hold down his hands, please.

04:53.585 --> 04:56.797
[narrator] I'm a public health doctor
who's to serve a three-year term

04:57.547 --> 05:03.053
in medically underserved areas
in lieu of regular military service.

05:03.136 --> 05:05.430
PUBLIC HEALTH DOCTOR

05:07.390 --> 05:08.975
It's a closed fracture in the left arm.

05:09.059 --> 05:10.477
Okay.

05:10.560 --> 05:14.523
-Can you feel anything in your fingertips?
-No, I can't. [groans]

05:14.606 --> 05:18.109
Sir, would you mind
if I sutured this laceration?

05:18.193 --> 05:20.487
Uh. Would you do that for me?

05:25.492 --> 05:26.493
[patient] Wait.

05:26.576 --> 05:27.577
Yes?

05:28.453 --> 05:30.288
Would this leave a scar on my face?

05:31.164 --> 05:32.749
I'm an aspiring actor.

05:33.542 --> 05:34.793
If I got a scar on my face…

05:35.377 --> 05:37.045
You don't have to worry about that.

05:37.128 --> 05:39.714
He's a board-certified plastic surgeon
at a university hospital.

05:39.798 --> 05:41.216
He'll make sure there's no scar.

05:41.299 --> 05:42.926
[sighs]

05:43.009 --> 05:44.803
-Thank you.
-Sure.

05:45.720 --> 05:47.639
-Please turn your head a little.
-Okay.

05:54.521 --> 05:56.523
[♪ gentle music playing]

07:25.028 --> 07:26.946
Make sure not to get any water on it.

07:27.030 --> 07:30.033
You'll have to get it dressed every day
until the stitches are removed.

07:30.784 --> 07:34.663
To be honest, I used to think
the PH docs were pathetic.

07:35.413 --> 07:37.999
I couldn't help but wonder
how they had become doctors

07:38.083 --> 07:40.085
when they couldn't even
do a drill properly.

07:40.168 --> 07:42.462
[chuckles] Well, we're more accustomed
to studying at a desk, so…

07:42.545 --> 07:44.339
But I was wrong.

07:44.964 --> 07:48.176
The way you ran over to us
without any hesitation…

07:49.594 --> 07:51.221
You were like superheroes.

07:51.304 --> 07:54.557
IT IS OUR DUTY
TO SAVE OUR COMRADES' LIVES

07:54.641 --> 07:55.684
Thank you.

07:55.767 --> 07:57.435
2ND TRAINING BATTALION BARRACKS

07:57.519 --> 07:59.312
Where are you thinking of applying?

08:00.313 --> 08:02.440
Well, it's not like
things would go my way,

08:02.524 --> 08:04.526
since it's all up to the luck of the draw.

08:04.609 --> 08:05.860
I'm fine anywhere but an island.

08:05.944 --> 08:07.654
True. Islands are the worst.

08:08.488 --> 08:11.366
But if you do end up going to one,
be wary of three things.

08:12.784 --> 08:14.911
Three things?

08:14.994 --> 08:16.371
What three things?

08:16.454 --> 08:17.872
It's just something I heard.

08:17.956 --> 08:20.959
They say there are three things
that'll make your life a living hell.

08:21.042 --> 08:24.379
Incidents, people, and love.

08:24.462 --> 08:27.340
And if you get caught up in all three,
you'll never escape.
STYLE
::cue()

08:29.592 --> 08:34.806
Incidents, people, and love?

08:37.851 --> 08:39.644
[officer 4] Trainees!

08:39.728 --> 08:41.271
Which one of you was chatting?

08:41.354 --> 08:43.523
-I'm sorry, sir!
-Why are you dressed like that?

08:43.606 --> 08:44.691
Where's your cap?

08:44.774 --> 08:46.860
My cap? Oh, my cap…

08:46.943 --> 08:48.069
[officer 4] Why, you little!

08:48.153 --> 08:50.780
-Down on the ground!
-[soldiers] Down on the ground!

08:51.906 --> 08:55.201
On one, "Dress code."
On two, "Violation." One!

08:55.285 --> 08:56.411
[all] Dress code!

08:56.494 --> 08:58.371
-Two!
-Violation!

08:58.455 --> 09:00.540
-One!
-Dress code!

09:00.623 --> 09:02.792
-Two!
-Violation!

09:02.876 --> 09:04.002
-One!
-Dress code!

09:04.085 --> 09:05.086
[doctor] No way.

09:05.962 --> 09:07.881
There's no way I'd end up on an island.

09:08.590 --> 09:10.759
I couldn't possibly be that unlucky.

09:17.599 --> 09:18.725
I…

09:19.392 --> 09:20.602
was that unlucky.

09:20.685 --> 09:22.062
[ship horn blowing]

09:22.145 --> 09:23.521
YEOPOONG MARINE TRANSPORT

09:23.605 --> 09:28.902
EPISODE 1
THE DOCTOR SENT TO THE ISLAND

09:29.527 --> 09:32.072
Wow, for real? Okay.

09:32.739 --> 09:34.741
I guess I should go.

09:37.869 --> 09:39.496
I really don't think I can do this.

09:39.579 --> 09:42.082
Seriously, I really don't think I can go.

09:42.916 --> 09:44.459
You have to go, dumbass.

09:44.542 --> 09:45.919
What else can you do?

09:48.588 --> 09:49.589
Oh, man…

09:50.090 --> 09:53.093
[phone buzzing]

09:58.681 --> 09:59.682
Hey, Gangseok.

09:59.766 --> 10:01.017
Are you leaving now?

10:01.101 --> 10:02.310
[doctor] Yeah.

10:02.393 --> 10:03.645
You're in for a rough time.

10:04.395 --> 10:06.606
-How about your meds?
-Not yet.

10:06.689 --> 10:09.651
Those meds can cause side effects
like memory loss, dizziness,

10:09.734 --> 10:13.279
and hallucinations,
so not taking them would be ideal.

10:13.363 --> 10:14.364
I know.

10:15.115 --> 10:18.409
You heard the news about Hwayeong, right?

10:20.203 --> 10:23.414
Hey, so things haven't changed
between you guys?

10:23.498 --> 10:25.500
It's been a long time since Seonu left.

10:26.584 --> 10:28.002
So much time has passed…

10:28.086 --> 10:29.546
So what if time has passed?

10:31.005 --> 10:33.383
Scars aren't something
that heal over time.

10:34.134 --> 10:35.260
Scars…

10:37.220 --> 10:38.596
are healed with money.

10:40.473 --> 10:43.268
If you're worried about my scars,
shut your mouth and open your wallet.

10:44.185 --> 10:46.271
-[Gangseok] Hello? Jiui.
-Yeah.

10:46.354 --> 10:48.356
-Good luck out there.
-Thanks, Gangseok.

10:48.439 --> 10:49.440
Sure.

10:50.567 --> 10:52.360
[ship horn blows]

10:53.820 --> 10:55.405
[♪ gentle music plays]

11:17.302 --> 11:21.431
[announcer on PA] The ship bound for
Pyeondongdo, Pyeondongdo is now departing.

11:21.514 --> 11:23.224
Go. You have to go, you crazy bastard.

11:23.308 --> 11:27.228
All remaining passengers,
please board the ship at this time.

11:27.312 --> 11:28.938
[♪ eerie music plays]

11:29.022 --> 11:33.276
The ship bound for Pyeondongdo,
Pyeondongdo is now departing.

11:33.860 --> 11:35.987
All remaining passengers…

11:40.366 --> 11:42.368
[distorted audio]

11:50.376 --> 11:52.378
[breathing heavily]

11:55.381 --> 11:56.716
Please…

11:58.259 --> 11:59.510
[panting]

12:01.054 --> 12:03.223
DO JI UI, M
ELLMARP

12:09.938 --> 12:11.481
[Jiui, normal] Two hours to Pyeondongdo.

12:14.859 --> 12:16.277
All I have to do is fall asleep.

12:17.570 --> 12:18.988
Nothing's going to happen.

12:20.031 --> 12:21.115
Nothing.
STYLE
::cue()

12:36.089 --> 12:40.385
[ship horn blows]

12:52.855 --> 12:55.233
[passengers chattering]

12:55.316 --> 12:56.901
[passenger 1] We need to get
our numbers straight.

12:56.985 --> 12:58.319
Excuse me, young man.

12:58.403 --> 12:59.404
Hey, young man.

12:59.487 --> 13:00.989
Hey, open your eyes.

13:01.698 --> 13:03.783
[passenger 2] Young man!

13:03.866 --> 13:07.078
There's something we'd like to ask you.

13:07.161 --> 13:09.205
[muffled] My friend here
didn't have any cash,

13:09.289 --> 13:12.000
so she agreed to pay us back later
and borrowed…

13:12.083 --> 13:13.334
[distorted dialogue]

13:15.336 --> 13:17.088
That leaves 3,000 won, right?

13:17.171 --> 13:18.381
[breathes heavily]

13:19.465 --> 13:20.466
[grunts]

13:21.092 --> 13:23.303
[♪ eerie music plays]

13:40.862 --> 13:41.863
[normal] That's…

13:42.905 --> 13:44.073
dangerous.

13:45.533 --> 13:47.326
[breathing heavily]

13:53.082 --> 13:54.375
[groans]

14:08.473 --> 14:09.932
Excuse me.

14:13.519 --> 14:15.021
Excuse me!

14:17.690 --> 14:19.484
That's dangerous. Get down from there now.

14:19.567 --> 14:21.069
-[ship horn blows]
-[Jiui] Whoa.

14:21.152 --> 14:23.071
Don't step any closer.

14:23.154 --> 14:25.031
Don't do it. Get down from there!

14:45.635 --> 14:46.636
Hey!

14:49.597 --> 14:50.723
No.

14:53.559 --> 14:56.020
[♪ somber music plays]

15:12.495 --> 15:13.788
Someone's fallen overboard!

15:13.871 --> 15:15.498
Stop the boat!

15:17.625 --> 15:19.669
I said someone's fallen overboard!

15:44.610 --> 15:46.612
[♪ ethereal music playing]

16:18.644 --> 16:19.687
[chuckles]
STYLE
::cue()

16:36.829 --> 16:40.333
Take three steps outside,
and you'll find fish everywhere.

16:40.416 --> 16:42.668
So why are you looking
at the fish inside a tank?

16:42.752 --> 16:45.713
Come on, these guys
are different from those guys.

16:46.631 --> 16:49.550
They're raised for consumption.
These guys are meant for observing.

16:49.634 --> 16:51.761
They're totally different.

16:52.929 --> 16:55.640
Why are you even ranking fish?

16:55.723 --> 16:58.059
Whether they live
in seawater or tap water,

16:58.142 --> 16:59.936
they all live in water just the same.

17:00.019 --> 17:03.314
Oh, right.
You saw my leave request, right?

17:03.397 --> 17:07.026
Hey, I told you to put in requests
at least three days in advance, didn't I?

17:07.109 --> 17:10.154
[clicks tongue] I'll take care of it
this time, but don't let it happen again.

17:11.197 --> 17:12.949
Okay. Thank you.

17:15.284 --> 17:16.661
[nurse 1] Granny.

17:16.744 --> 17:17.912
-Granny Sunja.
-[Sunja] Yes?

17:17.995 --> 17:19.664
-Let's have you go inside.
-Okay.

17:19.747 --> 17:21.207
-Is it that room?
-Yes.

17:21.290 --> 17:24.126
[nurse 1] I've opened the door,
so all you need to do is step inside.

17:24.210 --> 17:26.754
[nurse 2] We haven't heard from
the new doctor yet, have we?

17:26.837 --> 17:28.881
No. They said
the ferry already arrived, though.

17:28.965 --> 17:31.300
Mmm. Must've been a paddle boat.

17:31.384 --> 17:33.803
[scoffs] Think he might have gotten lost?

17:33.886 --> 17:36.055
A smart doctor getting lost?

17:36.138 --> 17:39.141
On this tiny island?

17:39.225 --> 17:41.269
I'm telling you,
he's definitely taken a detour.

17:41.894 --> 17:43.354
Should I try giving him a call?

17:43.437 --> 17:44.438
I'll do it.

17:46.023 --> 17:49.026
I'm going to give him an earful and
really straighten him out. [clears throat]

17:49.110 --> 17:50.486
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

17:50.570 --> 17:52.029
[line ringing]

17:53.281 --> 17:56.701
[phone ringing]

17:56.784 --> 17:58.703
[snores, grunts]

17:58.786 --> 17:59.787
Damn it.

18:05.626 --> 18:07.086
Hello?

18:07.169 --> 18:08.379
[nurse 2] Dr. Do Jiui?

18:09.672 --> 18:10.881
Yes, who is this?

18:11.549 --> 18:14.010
I'm calling from
the Pyeondongdo Public Health Center.

18:15.386 --> 18:17.638
What is the Pyeondongdo
Public Health Center?

18:18.848 --> 18:20.600
[knocks on door]

18:22.101 --> 18:23.686
Dr. Do Jiui?

18:24.437 --> 18:26.105
[gasps, breathes heavily]

18:28.941 --> 18:30.943
[♪ playful music plays]

18:35.406 --> 18:39.076
Goodness, I had no idea
you were already here.

18:39.160 --> 18:41.412
We've been looking all over for you.

18:41.495 --> 18:42.788
Ugh.

18:45.666 --> 18:47.418
[stutters] What happened?

18:47.501 --> 18:49.045
[stutters] How about that woman?

18:49.128 --> 18:50.630
Is she still alive?

18:50.713 --> 18:51.922
What is he rambling about?

18:52.423 --> 18:54.842
[chuckles] I guess you must've had
a pretty wild dream.

18:55.885 --> 18:57.094
-A dream?
-Oh, my.

18:57.178 --> 18:59.805
I heard someone passed out on the ferry,

18:59.889 --> 19:02.016
so I thought it might be
a tourist or a fisherman

19:02.099 --> 19:03.684
who had drunk too much.

19:03.768 --> 19:06.812
Never did I guess
it would be our doctor. [chuckles]

19:07.855 --> 19:09.857
Wait, so that was really a dream?

19:09.940 --> 19:13.027
Mmm. That's enough.
It's time for you to wake up.

19:13.110 --> 19:14.695
I'll show you the health center.

19:14.779 --> 19:17.990
You'll be here for a year,
so you should get familiar with the place.

19:19.116 --> 19:20.576
-Right.
-Come on.

19:24.664 --> 19:25.665
Here.

19:26.332 --> 19:29.418
[yelps] He's coming out right on time.
Please introduce yourselves.

19:29.502 --> 19:32.296
This is Dr. Yong Jucheon
from the Korean Medicine ward.

19:32.380 --> 19:34.507
This here is our new surgeon, Dr. Do Jiui.

19:35.091 --> 19:36.092
Hello.

19:36.175 --> 19:37.468
Ooh!

19:37.551 --> 19:39.261
You were carried in earlier, right?

19:39.345 --> 19:42.264
[chuckles] So you're a doctor
assigned here, huh?

19:42.348 --> 19:43.849
We're really glad to have you.

19:43.933 --> 19:45.351
Hold on.

19:45.434 --> 19:47.019
If you're a doctor, here.

19:47.770 --> 19:50.314
-Sorry?
-[Jucheon] I'm asking for your number.

19:50.398 --> 19:54.026
It's hard adjusting to life here
when you've arrived from the city.

19:54.110 --> 19:57.196
One for regional PH docs,
one for us here, our public health center,

19:57.279 --> 19:59.490
Youth Association, Women's Association…

19:59.573 --> 20:01.575
Anyway, I'll invite you
to all the group chats.

20:01.659 --> 20:03.869
People live here
just like any other place.

20:03.953 --> 20:05.913
How different could it be?

20:05.996 --> 20:09.375
Stop making such a big fuss,
and take it slow with stuff like that.

20:09.458 --> 20:11.419
We haven't even shown him his office yet.

20:11.502 --> 20:13.629
Your office is that way.

20:13.713 --> 20:15.047
Exam room number one.

20:15.131 --> 20:17.091
We gave you the biggest room.

20:17.174 --> 20:20.136
Since you're a medical specialist.
[chuckles]

20:20.219 --> 20:22.805
Here, this way. You should see your room.

20:25.349 --> 20:27.601
A mercury sphygmomanometer.
STYLE
::cue()

20:28.894 --> 20:31.105
It's a bit outdated, isn't it? [chuckles]

20:31.772 --> 20:35.317
We do bring it up every year,
but nothing ever changes.

20:35.901 --> 20:39.155
I know it's rather shoddy compared
to the university hospitals in Seoul,

20:39.238 --> 20:42.074
but I doubt you'll have any major issues.

20:42.158 --> 20:45.244
The patients who visit our center

20:45.327 --> 20:48.581
don't come here
because of anything bad in particular,

20:48.664 --> 20:50.374
but because of chronic illnesses.

20:50.458 --> 20:51.876
Blood pressure, diabetes, and arthritis.

20:51.959 --> 20:55.421
They just live with those conditions
their whole lives. [chuckles]

20:55.504 --> 20:58.716
One granny said she hurt everywhere
except her eyebrows. [laughs]

20:59.800 --> 21:01.594
We should still get a new BP monitor.

21:04.096 --> 21:05.514
Right.

21:13.397 --> 21:15.816
[clears throat] You've seen
pretty much everything now.

21:15.900 --> 21:17.651
Should I get you something to drink?

21:18.235 --> 21:19.904
No, I just want to wash up right now.

21:19.987 --> 21:22.740
Uh. Here, your key.

21:22.823 --> 21:24.200
Right.

21:24.283 --> 21:28.204
To get to your room,
go up like this, go up like this,

21:28.287 --> 21:30.831
then go up like this,
and it's the first room on the left.

21:33.709 --> 21:34.710
[grunts]

21:35.586 --> 21:37.087
[exhales] Man, that's a lot better.

21:37.922 --> 21:38.923
[chittering]

21:39.006 --> 21:41.008
[♪ whimsical music plays]

21:48.849 --> 21:50.267
[chittering]

22:00.611 --> 22:01.612
[yelps]

22:03.239 --> 22:04.782
[grunts]

22:09.578 --> 22:11.038
[panting]

22:15.709 --> 22:16.836
What happened?

22:16.919 --> 22:18.462
There was a centipede this big!

22:18.546 --> 22:20.464
It fell on my face and… [panting]

22:20.548 --> 22:21.632
My goodness.

22:21.715 --> 22:24.176
And here I was thinking
it was something serious.

22:24.260 --> 22:26.303
I bet the centipede
was more startled than you.

22:26.387 --> 22:30.266
Centipedes aren't the only things here.
And they're tame compared to the rest.

22:30.349 --> 22:32.977
Snakes, house centipedes, spiders…

22:33.644 --> 22:36.313
Just think of them as your roommates.

22:36.397 --> 22:38.065
BUG SPRAY

22:49.493 --> 22:50.744
[shushes]

22:51.787 --> 22:53.831
[coughs]

23:14.894 --> 23:17.146
Oh. This isn't mine.

23:30.284 --> 23:31.285
No way.

23:32.328 --> 23:33.704
That woman with the bottle?

23:33.787 --> 23:35.039
[grunting]

23:38.751 --> 23:40.836
[panting]

23:45.841 --> 23:47.259
What now?

23:47.343 --> 23:48.594
Another bug?

23:48.677 --> 23:49.678
No.

23:49.762 --> 23:52.723
I think my suitcase got swapped,
and I'm not sure what to do.

23:52.806 --> 23:54.642
It's one thing after another
with this guy.

23:54.725 --> 23:57.937
For that, you'll have to go
to the village hall.

23:58.020 --> 24:00.648
If you tell
the Youth Association members there,

24:00.731 --> 24:02.816
they'll help you out
with just about anything.

24:02.900 --> 24:03.901
Go there.

24:03.984 --> 24:06.070
The village hall? Okay. Thank you.
STYLE
::cue()

24:06.153 --> 24:08.155
[♪ amusing music plays]

24:09.323 --> 24:10.324
Oh, man.

24:24.797 --> 24:27.174
[Jiui exclaims]

24:27.257 --> 24:30.135
Are you kidding me right now? [coughs]

24:33.430 --> 24:35.724
What's a car like that
doing on an island like this?

24:36.225 --> 24:38.435
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

24:38.519 --> 24:40.396
-Thanks for your hard work.
-Sure.

24:41.230 --> 24:42.564
How did the home visit go?

24:43.315 --> 24:45.818
How was the granny doing?
Is she better now?

24:45.901 --> 24:47.236
Yes, she's better now.

24:49.363 --> 24:53.659
Ms. Hwang, what exactly
are the criteria for home visits?

24:53.742 --> 24:55.077
What do you mean by that?

24:55.661 --> 24:57.913
I just don't think it's fair
that even the patients

24:57.997 --> 25:00.165
who are perfectly capable
of getting around

25:00.249 --> 25:01.625
get to apply for home visits.

25:01.709 --> 25:02.876
[Ms. Hwang] Ah.

25:03.502 --> 25:06.505
Right, it can be unfair.

25:06.588 --> 25:08.590
But such are human affairs.

25:08.674 --> 25:11.552
Not everything can be
perfectly fair, you know?

25:11.635 --> 25:12.928
Yes.

25:14.430 --> 25:16.849
Then I'll be turning down home visits.

25:17.516 --> 25:18.517
What?

25:18.600 --> 25:21.937
To my understanding, PH docs
aren't obligated to perform home visits.

25:29.945 --> 25:32.114
Wow, that guy…

25:32.197 --> 25:34.450
PYEONDONGDO VILLAGE HALL

25:35.367 --> 25:39.204
So, your suitcase got mixed up
with someone else's on the ferry?

25:39.288 --> 25:41.415
Yes. I think it got mixed up
with some woman's.

25:41.498 --> 25:43.250
She had short hair.

25:44.793 --> 25:46.295
By the way,

25:46.378 --> 25:49.256
weren't there any accidents
involving one of the passengers?

25:49.339 --> 25:51.675
Like someone falling into the water or…

25:51.759 --> 25:54.344
We've never had accidents
involving passengers.

25:54.428 --> 25:57.931
Our ferry, the Hansol No. 3,
has been accident-free for 20 years.

25:59.850 --> 26:01.143
Hold on.

26:01.226 --> 26:04.188
It must have gotten mixed up
with Granny Mija's granddaughter's.

26:05.439 --> 26:06.690
Sorry? Granddaughter?

26:06.774 --> 26:10.319
Oh, my. You must really
not remember, Doctor.

26:11.361 --> 26:15.324
The one who carried you on her back
was Granny Mija's granddaughter.

26:15.407 --> 26:17.159
-Granddaughter?
-But anyway,

26:17.242 --> 26:19.578
if you're a doctor, why are you so feeble?

26:19.661 --> 26:22.289
Hey, quit it!

26:22.372 --> 26:24.041
That's how your suitcase got mixed up.

26:24.124 --> 26:26.835
So the one who carried me was a woman?

26:30.589 --> 26:33.425
I mean, all these houses
have red rooftops.

26:34.510 --> 26:36.929
Which red rooftop were they talking about?

26:39.681 --> 26:42.226
And what does "follow the road
and go straight" mean?

26:42.309 --> 26:43.936
I've been walking straight forever.

26:44.019 --> 26:46.522
[bypasser 1 screaming] Help!

26:47.523 --> 26:48.774
Move!

26:52.111 --> 26:53.612
Run!

26:53.695 --> 26:55.155
[♪ gentle music plays]

26:56.448 --> 27:00.369
[barking, growling]
STYLE
::cue()

27:40.492 --> 27:42.953
-Hurry! This way!
-Run!

27:47.124 --> 27:48.959
[shrieking]

27:49.877 --> 27:52.129
-[screaming]
-No!

28:00.888 --> 28:03.515
Deokgu!

28:03.599 --> 28:05.893
Goodness me, where did you go?

28:05.976 --> 28:08.687
Oh, no, Deokgu!

28:08.770 --> 28:11.064
I'm sorry!

28:11.148 --> 28:13.066
I was wondering where you had run off to.

28:13.150 --> 28:15.152
-Come here. Gosh, I'm sorry.
-Deokgu?

28:15.235 --> 28:17.779
-Deokgu?
-Where have you been?

28:18.697 --> 28:20.157
Come here.

28:20.240 --> 28:21.241
You bad boy. Let's go.

28:21.325 --> 28:22.743
-Come on.
-Auntie!

28:24.036 --> 28:26.580
[stutters] You're Hari, aren't you?

28:26.663 --> 28:31.418
-[yelps] Auntie! I'm so happy to see you!
-Oh, my!

28:31.501 --> 28:33.003
Have you been well?

28:33.086 --> 28:34.379
What are you doing here?

28:34.463 --> 28:35.464
[giggles]

28:35.964 --> 28:38.216
Deokgu's grown so big. Hi, Deokgu.

28:38.300 --> 28:40.177
-[Hari] You're still cute.
-That's a friendly dog.

28:51.897 --> 28:53.607
[grunts] Gosh, I'm sorry.

28:55.609 --> 28:58.612
I must have taken your suitcase
because I was so out of it. [chuckles]

28:59.279 --> 29:00.489
Check this one too.

29:00.572 --> 29:01.907
I'm sure it's mine.

29:01.990 --> 29:03.408
Well, you should still check.

29:03.492 --> 29:05.661
I opened it briefly.
The lock code was the same.

29:05.744 --> 29:08.580
Wow, then I guess
we must have the same birthday.

29:09.665 --> 29:11.166
November 6th?

29:11.249 --> 29:12.626
No, January 16th.

29:12.709 --> 29:14.127
I see. [chuckles]

29:28.308 --> 29:30.018
Oh, my. Why are these…

29:34.439 --> 29:36.525
MEDICAL PATCH
NARCOTIC PAINKILLERS

29:36.608 --> 29:38.193
CHAVOXIFEN
CHAVOXIFEN CITRATE

29:38.276 --> 29:39.653
[Jiui] "Chavoxifen"?

29:40.737 --> 29:43.699
That's a targeted agent.

29:44.574 --> 29:46.576
[♪ somber music plays]

29:54.084 --> 29:55.794
Looks like everything's here.

30:00.257 --> 30:02.718
[chittering]

30:02.801 --> 30:04.011
[exclaims]

30:04.094 --> 30:05.721
-That's where it was.
-What's wrong?

30:05.804 --> 30:07.723
-Damn it.
-What?

30:09.141 --> 30:11.893
-Goodness, let me get that for you.
-Okay.

30:18.233 --> 30:19.901
Good. [chuckles]

30:21.028 --> 30:22.112
It's fine.

30:25.240 --> 30:26.616
All done.

30:26.700 --> 30:27.701
Right.

30:28.535 --> 30:31.413
Mine's good to go.
Shouldn't you check yours?

30:33.623 --> 30:34.750
Right.

30:44.843 --> 30:47.345
[♪ soft guitar plays]

30:53.685 --> 30:54.936
Oh, right.

30:56.688 --> 30:58.398
This also belongs to you, right?

30:58.482 --> 31:00.192
ELLMARP

31:00.275 --> 31:03.111
[sighs] Thank you.
STYLE
::cue()

31:05.155 --> 31:06.823
Don't take that medication.

31:08.658 --> 31:10.827
I don't think it agrees with you.

31:10.911 --> 31:12.913
You were in serious danger
on the ferry earlier.

31:13.580 --> 31:14.581
[scoffs]

31:15.499 --> 31:16.500
Wait…

31:17.501 --> 31:20.837
Look who's talking about being in danger.

31:20.921 --> 31:22.297
[stutters] What?

31:22.380 --> 31:24.174
What were you doing up there anyway?

31:24.257 --> 31:26.718
Were you trying to kill yourself?

31:26.802 --> 31:27.803
Me?

31:28.512 --> 31:29.513
Why on earth would I--

31:29.596 --> 31:32.099
I got into this whole mess
because I tried to save you.

31:32.682 --> 31:35.769
[chuckles] What the heck
are you talking about?

31:37.354 --> 31:39.356
[♪ intriguing music plays]

31:41.149 --> 31:43.527
Ms. Mija, it's so pretty out here!

31:43.610 --> 31:45.112
Check out the ocean.

31:45.195 --> 31:49.407
Goodness, what beauty is there
in something I see every day?

31:49.491 --> 31:52.911
To me, you're the prettiest thing
in the world, Hari.

31:52.994 --> 31:56.915
[Hari] Hey, I take after my grandma.
Of course I'm pretty.

31:56.998 --> 31:58.083
[groaning]

31:59.084 --> 32:00.460
[Hari] Grandma, have you eaten yet?

32:04.673 --> 32:06.883
-My cardigan went flying.
-[Jiui groaning]

32:06.967 --> 32:09.845
-[Hari] I'll just have to get a new one.
-Hey, don't!

32:10.512 --> 32:11.847
[Hari yelps]

32:11.930 --> 32:14.516
No, don't!

32:14.599 --> 32:15.600
What?

32:15.684 --> 32:18.770
-Don't go.
-Oh, no. You have to be careful.

32:18.854 --> 32:20.230
It's dangerous up there!

32:20.313 --> 32:22.482
-Over here!
-What?

32:22.566 --> 32:25.277
[Jiui] I need help over here!

32:26.278 --> 32:27.362
Someone…

32:27.445 --> 32:29.531
Someone's fallen into the water!

32:29.614 --> 32:32.117
I think we have to stop the boat!

32:32.200 --> 32:33.827
What did you say?

32:33.910 --> 32:36.746
-I'll… I'll save her.
-[Hari] Careful!

32:36.830 --> 32:38.874
-I'll save you!
-Who are you trying to save?

32:40.208 --> 32:42.502
Oh, no. What do I do?

32:42.586 --> 32:44.588
-I'll save you!
-Wait!

32:44.671 --> 32:46.923
-[Jiui] No… Damn it.
-Just hold on!

33:07.611 --> 33:08.904
[scoffs]

33:09.696 --> 33:10.822
[stutters] I did that?

33:10.906 --> 33:13.325
[ship horn blows]

33:13.408 --> 33:16.912
[panting] I shouldn't have
knocked him out like that.

33:17.579 --> 33:20.123
Gosh, he's so freaking heavy. [panting]

33:21.833 --> 33:25.170
Excuse me, please wake up.

33:25.253 --> 33:27.380
You really don't remember anything?

33:29.966 --> 33:32.302
I don't remember that at all. I don't.

33:36.264 --> 33:37.807
Are you better now?

33:37.891 --> 33:39.517
Gosh. I'm totally…

33:41.811 --> 33:43.480
-Are you leaving?
-Of course!

33:45.398 --> 33:46.399
[Hari] Take care!

33:49.444 --> 33:50.445
Oh, no.

33:58.536 --> 33:59.871
What's with that guy?

34:05.710 --> 34:07.963
[♪ gentle music plays]
STYLE
::cue()

34:08.046 --> 34:10.131
-[Mija] Yeah, on that side.
-[Hari] Yes.

34:10.215 --> 34:11.633
[Mija] Did you return his suitcase?

34:11.716 --> 34:12.717
[Hari] Yeah.

34:13.718 --> 34:15.679
And he didn't say anything weird?

34:15.762 --> 34:18.139
Sounded like he wasn't normal.

34:18.223 --> 34:19.557
Yeah, he's a total weirdo.

34:19.641 --> 34:22.727
You said you were going back
to the mainland again tomorrow.

34:22.811 --> 34:25.105
Why did you have to move your bags today

34:25.188 --> 34:27.190
and get mixed up with a guy like that?

34:27.274 --> 34:30.068
Tomorrow will come
with tomorrow's share of baggage.

34:30.151 --> 34:33.571
Why did you even come
all the way back to this island?

34:33.655 --> 34:35.824
Let's hurry. Mom and Dad must be hungry.

34:35.907 --> 34:38.618
Look at you. Fine, let's do that.

34:38.702 --> 34:39.703
Here we go.

34:42.914 --> 34:43.915
What the heck?

34:45.292 --> 34:47.002
Why's this thing open?

34:49.504 --> 34:51.923
No idea. I wonder why it was open.

34:52.007 --> 34:53.967
You drank from it, didn't you?

34:55.051 --> 34:56.052
[stammers]

34:56.136 --> 34:58.680
I only did it because I was thirsty.

34:58.763 --> 35:02.267
Goodness me. Who did you get that from?

35:02.350 --> 35:04.311
I got it all from you, Granny.

35:04.394 --> 35:06.354
-How are you so cute?
-[Hari giggles]

35:06.438 --> 35:08.273
I also got that all from you, Granny.

35:08.356 --> 35:10.275
My, my, you precious thing.

35:16.489 --> 35:19.367
Making up stories
just because I don't remember.

35:21.453 --> 35:23.913
Does she not realize
I ended up like that because of her?

35:23.997 --> 35:25.248
Man, this is just…

35:28.835 --> 35:31.713
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

35:31.796 --> 35:33.798
[♪ whimsical music playing]

35:35.008 --> 35:36.009
What the…

35:36.885 --> 35:39.429
-What's this car doing here?
-[engine revving]

35:44.100 --> 35:45.185
[grunts]

35:48.063 --> 35:49.064
[groans]

35:53.109 --> 35:54.110
BATHROOM

35:55.779 --> 35:57.781
[♪ sultry music playing]

36:10.502 --> 36:11.878
[music ends]

36:16.424 --> 36:19.719
I'm sorry. I thought
there was no one in here…

36:21.471 --> 36:23.348
You're the doctor who came today, right?

36:24.557 --> 36:26.559
Yes. I'm Do Jiui.

36:28.812 --> 36:29.938
I'm Hyeon Chiyeon.

36:34.526 --> 36:36.027
I heard you were carried here.

36:39.489 --> 36:40.824
I don't recall that.

36:42.659 --> 36:45.620
That's a relief.
I look forward to working with you.

36:51.000 --> 36:52.168
What the heck was that?

37:02.178 --> 37:03.179
[grunts]

37:06.391 --> 37:07.392
[sighs]

37:12.147 --> 37:14.149
[♪ sentimental music playing]

37:24.534 --> 37:25.535
Doctor.

37:27.287 --> 37:28.455
Aren't you hungry?

37:28.538 --> 37:31.291
You should treat us all
since it's your first day here.
STYLE
::cue()

37:33.168 --> 37:34.294
-Me?
-Yes.

37:34.377 --> 37:36.880
Dr. Chiyeon is waiting for you,
so hurry and come outside.

37:40.341 --> 37:41.843
Why should I be treating them?

37:42.552 --> 37:45.597
CLIFFSIDE RAW FISH RESTAURANT
BEST RESTAURANT IN PYEONDONGDO

37:45.680 --> 37:46.848
Hello.

37:48.558 --> 37:50.602
Auntie, we're here!

37:50.685 --> 37:52.145
[Geumja] Oh, you're here?

37:53.688 --> 37:55.482
It's so hot.

37:58.067 --> 37:59.694
-Oh, my.
-Huh?

37:59.778 --> 38:01.196
It's you again.

38:01.905 --> 38:04.449
-That was quite startling, wasn't it?
-Yes.

38:04.532 --> 38:06.576
-You two have already met?
-Yes.

38:06.659 --> 38:09.412
-[stutters] There was a minor incident.
-Ah.

38:09.996 --> 38:12.957
Auntie, we'll have the dish
that got rave reviews on that TV show.

38:13.041 --> 38:15.376
-The one we ordered in advance, please.
-Of course.

38:15.460 --> 38:17.045
-Just give me a moment.
-[Jucheon] Okay.

38:19.464 --> 38:21.299
What do you specialize in, Doctor?

38:22.217 --> 38:24.928
-Plastic surgery.
-Wow.

38:25.011 --> 38:28.223
You must have done very well in school.
Plastic surgery is so popular.

38:28.306 --> 38:29.307
Yes, well…

38:29.390 --> 38:32.060
You haven't chosen
your specialty yet, right?

38:32.143 --> 38:33.895
-That's right.
-Hmm.

38:33.978 --> 38:35.438
How about a plastic surgery clinic?

38:35.522 --> 38:38.691
If you opened a clinic in Gangnam,
I bet people would line up asking you

38:38.775 --> 38:41.069
to fix them up
to look like you. [chuckles]

38:42.320 --> 38:43.613
Hmm.

38:43.696 --> 38:45.198
I don't know.

38:45.281 --> 38:47.659
I'm not a huge fan of plastic surgeons.

38:48.243 --> 38:50.036
They just come across as money-grubbers.

38:51.538 --> 38:52.539
What did you say?

38:53.748 --> 38:55.834
Ah. I sure am hungry.

38:57.377 --> 38:59.003
Right to my face? Really?

38:59.087 --> 39:02.966
Here it comes, our signature dish.

39:04.384 --> 39:06.135
-Here you are.
-[Jucheon] Wow.

39:08.596 --> 39:10.598
[♪ intriguing music playing]

39:16.396 --> 39:18.022
[Geumja sighs]

39:20.608 --> 39:21.609
[Geumja exclaims]

39:22.360 --> 39:23.945
-Uh…
-It looks so good.

39:26.573 --> 39:27.574
[gags]

39:28.324 --> 39:29.951
-Thank you.
-[Geumja chuckles]

39:32.287 --> 39:34.163
And here's one for you, Doctor.

39:34.247 --> 39:35.748
Hurry up and eat.

39:35.832 --> 39:37.917
This is the only restaurant
in Pyeondongdo.

39:38.543 --> 39:42.088
If you don't hype it up,
you'll starve to death.

39:44.007 --> 39:45.550
[Geumja] There you go.

39:46.551 --> 39:49.220
-Yes, thank you.
-[Geumja] Enjoy.

39:51.723 --> 39:53.933
-[Geumja] Here.
-[Jucheon] Thank you.

39:54.684 --> 39:59.105
I don't know
if it'll suit your taste, Doctor.

40:00.189 --> 40:01.190
Hurry.

40:01.274 --> 40:04.485
Your only source of sustenance
for a whole year rests on it.

40:10.074 --> 40:11.159
[sighs]

40:14.370 --> 40:15.663
[chuckles] Eat up.

40:15.747 --> 40:18.750
[♪ tense music playing]

40:26.841 --> 40:29.344
-[Jiui exclaims]
-Eh?

40:29.427 --> 40:31.054
[Jucheon chuckles]

40:33.056 --> 40:34.057
[landline ringing]

40:38.645 --> 40:40.813
[Geumja] Yes, this is Cliffside.

40:40.897 --> 40:41.898
Yes.

40:42.565 --> 40:43.566
What?

40:44.067 --> 40:45.777
They're all here.

40:45.860 --> 40:46.861
Okay.

40:47.695 --> 40:50.698
The chief is asking for one doctor
back at the center…

40:50.782 --> 40:52.408
-I'll go.
-[Jucheon] What?

40:52.492 --> 40:54.077
But it's your first day.

40:54.160 --> 40:56.913
What can I say? I'm a workaholic.
I'll finish it when I get back.
STYLE
::cue()

40:59.457 --> 41:01.459
[ship horn blares in distance]

41:07.799 --> 41:09.384
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

41:10.969 --> 41:12.095
Mr. Park.

41:12.178 --> 41:13.179
CLOSED

41:13.262 --> 41:14.514
Ah!

41:14.597 --> 41:18.059
Oh, Doctor. Did you find your suitcase?

41:18.142 --> 41:21.396
Yes, thanks to you.
But can you tell me how you're sick?

41:21.479 --> 41:26.526
[sighs] I think I have indigestion.
My chest is really stuffy.

41:26.609 --> 41:28.778
So, give me some Umetazole.

41:29.404 --> 41:31.239
-Umetazole?
-Ah.

41:31.739 --> 41:33.533
I think I have a bad case of indigestion.

41:33.616 --> 41:36.536
So bad that I threw up
everything I ate for breakfast.

41:37.161 --> 41:40.331
I have fishing customers coming,
so I have to get going right away.

41:40.415 --> 41:42.000
Please hurry and give it to me.

41:42.667 --> 41:45.044
Let's get inside
so I can take a look at you first.

41:45.128 --> 41:46.879
-Let's take this inside.
-Okay.

41:47.463 --> 41:48.881
[Chunsik groans]

41:50.133 --> 41:52.218
[sniffles] Here.

41:52.301 --> 41:53.720
The left side.

41:53.803 --> 41:55.805
My left arm's also really sore.

41:55.888 --> 41:57.515
It's killing me.

41:57.598 --> 41:59.767
Does it feel as if someone's wringing it?

41:59.851 --> 42:02.270
Yes. It does kind of feel like that.

42:02.979 --> 42:05.982
I must have serious indigestion.

42:06.065 --> 42:09.402
Just give me Umetazole.
I'll be fine once I take it.

42:09.485 --> 42:11.946
-I've always taken it.
-Let me take your blood pressure.

42:13.489 --> 42:15.033
Hey, now.

42:15.116 --> 42:18.036
I have indigestion.
Why even bother taking my blood pressure?

42:18.119 --> 42:20.121
[breathing heavily]

42:34.594 --> 42:37.096
[air hissing]

42:37.805 --> 42:39.807
[♪ tense music playing]

42:42.518 --> 42:45.271
[Jiui] Stuffiness in his left chest,
trouble breathing,

42:45.855 --> 42:49.233
chest pains that feel as though
someone's wringing his chest,

42:49.317 --> 42:54.447
high blood pressure, nausea,
and even referred pain in the left arm.

42:55.698 --> 42:57.075
All signs point to an MI.

42:57.158 --> 42:59.702
MI: MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION

43:06.417 --> 43:08.127
[inhales deeply] Wait here for a moment.

43:08.878 --> 43:09.879
[Chunsik] Okay.

43:27.897 --> 43:28.898
UMETAZOLE

43:33.277 --> 43:35.655
-Can you try taking this?
-Huh?

43:36.864 --> 43:38.950
[Jiui] Put it under your tongue,
and let it melt.

43:40.076 --> 43:41.077
Okay.

43:42.829 --> 43:43.830
[sighs]

43:45.206 --> 43:48.543
[breathing heavily]

43:52.255 --> 43:53.256
[exhales deeply]

43:55.174 --> 43:56.592
[sighs]

44:03.182 --> 44:04.642
[Chunsik groans]

44:05.143 --> 44:07.478
[breathes deeply]

44:09.188 --> 44:10.189
What the…

44:11.149 --> 44:12.942
I feel better already.

44:13.568 --> 44:15.319
[Jiui] He wasn't supposed to feel better.

44:15.403 --> 44:18.739
The fact that the NTG worked
within minutes means

44:19.323 --> 44:22.618
there's a higher than 80% chance that
we're looking at a myocardial infarction.
STYLE
::cue()

44:22.702 --> 44:25.288
PATIENT RECORD QUERY
MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION, NTG

44:25.371 --> 44:29.083
I thought you were a weakling
because a girl carried you here,

44:29.167 --> 44:31.294
but you're an amazing doctor. [chuckles]

44:31.377 --> 44:33.921
Pyeondongdo has nothing
to worry about now.

44:34.005 --> 44:38.509
If anything troubles you during your stay,
feel free to tell me about it.

44:39.260 --> 44:42.013
Now, I've got urgent business
to attend to, so I'll--

44:42.096 --> 44:44.015
No, you shouldn't leave right now.

44:44.098 --> 44:45.474
Why?

44:45.558 --> 44:47.268
That wasn't digestive medicine.

44:47.351 --> 44:49.353
It was a drug
for myocardial infarction patients.

44:50.188 --> 44:52.148
The fact that your condition improved

44:52.231 --> 44:55.568
means there's a higher than 80% chance
of you getting a heart attack.

44:55.651 --> 44:57.320
We have to get you to a big hospital.

44:57.403 --> 45:01.490
Oh, come on.
I see our new doctor's a total worrywart.

45:01.574 --> 45:04.076
A big hospital? Please, I'll be fine!

45:04.160 --> 45:06.204
I'm telling you, you have to go right now!

45:06.287 --> 45:08.956
Don't worry. I know my body best.

45:09.040 --> 45:10.082
Mr. Park!

45:10.166 --> 45:11.500
Move aside!

45:11.584 --> 45:14.545
If I get hit with a fee for bailing,
will you take responsibility?

45:14.629 --> 45:16.839
Keep this up
and something bad will happen to you.

45:16.923 --> 45:18.257
Geez. [sighs]

45:18.341 --> 45:22.345
Doctor, you said there was an 80% chance
of me getting a heart attack, right?

45:22.428 --> 45:25.223
But there's a 100% chance
of my fishing customers coming!

45:26.390 --> 45:27.767
-[sighs]
-Fine.

45:27.850 --> 45:31.229
I'll just give my customers a ride,
then go to a hospital, so move.

45:31.312 --> 45:32.772
You could end up passing away.

45:32.855 --> 45:34.065
What do you mean, pass…

45:39.820 --> 45:40.821
What now?

45:42.073 --> 45:43.074
Pass away?

45:43.783 --> 45:44.825
Yes.

45:48.037 --> 45:50.414
[exhales sharply] That's no good.

45:51.624 --> 45:52.625
What am I to do?

45:53.626 --> 45:54.627
So…

45:55.169 --> 45:57.213
You're saying I have to go no matter what?

46:03.052 --> 46:04.553
Okay.

46:04.637 --> 46:06.514
I should listen to you.

46:06.597 --> 46:09.267
Take a seat outside,
and I'll get right back to you.

46:09.350 --> 46:11.978
I guess I'll do that.

46:22.280 --> 46:23.281
[line ringing]

46:26.701 --> 46:28.786
Yes, Ms. Hwang.
We have an emergency patient.

46:28.869 --> 46:30.913
He's a myocardial infarction patient.
I'll…

46:31.497 --> 46:33.040
What? A chopper?

46:35.001 --> 46:36.585
Mr. Park, they're sending a chopper…

46:40.214 --> 46:41.215
Mr. Park?

46:47.430 --> 46:48.431
Mr. Park?

46:52.977 --> 46:54.312
Damn it.

46:54.979 --> 46:57.481
Trust me, I know my own body best.

47:00.901 --> 47:03.404
Goodness, I'm going to miss my customers.

47:06.365 --> 47:10.161
What do you mean
the patient's gone missing?

47:10.244 --> 47:12.413
He slipped out
while I was on the phone with you…

47:12.496 --> 47:14.623
-[gasps]
-What about the chopper?

47:14.707 --> 47:17.752
If we call one with no patient,
our center will be penalized.

47:17.835 --> 47:19.045
[Jiui] He'll get on that chopper.

47:19.128 --> 47:23.257
Given his response to NTG,
he may end up having a heart attack.

47:23.341 --> 47:25.426
So let's find him as quickly as we can.

47:26.010 --> 47:27.845
Is he not picking up his phone?

47:27.928 --> 47:29.930
Why isn't he answering his phone?

47:31.390 --> 47:33.476
-[stammers] The fishing boat.
-What?

47:33.559 --> 47:35.227
He said he had fishing customers.

47:35.311 --> 47:36.562
-Let's go!
-Let's hurry.

47:37.813 --> 47:39.023
Mr. Park!

47:39.899 --> 47:40.983
Mr. Park!

47:41.067 --> 47:42.068
Mr. Park!

47:43.903 --> 47:44.904
Mr. Park!
STYLE
::cue()

47:44.987 --> 47:46.030
Mr. Park!

47:48.949 --> 47:52.036
-Mr. Park!
-Mr. Park. Are you okay?

47:52.119 --> 47:53.746
You have to come with us right now.

47:53.829 --> 47:55.498
What brings you all here?

47:55.581 --> 47:57.416
Doesn't your body feel kind of iffy?

47:57.500 --> 48:01.337
Why the hell did you all follow me here?
I told you I'm fine, didn't I?

48:01.420 --> 48:03.297
I know my body best!

48:03.381 --> 48:06.133
-But still, you should…
-Mr. Park, that's all temporary.

48:06.217 --> 48:07.426
-You--
-I've heard enough.

48:07.510 --> 48:10.304
Just go about your business. I said, go!

48:10.388 --> 48:12.348
-I'm hella busy, okay?
-Okay.

48:12.431 --> 48:13.933
Then just a quick check.

48:14.016 --> 48:17.061
I'm fine! Just go.

48:17.144 --> 48:19.146
Hello, sir, come this way.

48:19.230 --> 48:20.773
This way. Get on the boat.

48:20.856 --> 48:23.651
-I said go away.
-Okay.

48:23.734 --> 48:25.069
I'm fine!

48:25.152 --> 48:26.779
-Okay.
-Here, get in.

48:26.862 --> 48:28.280
-This one, right?
-Yes.

48:29.240 --> 48:31.325
Scram! Stop blocking the way!

48:31.409 --> 48:32.701
Gosh, we're leaving.

48:32.785 --> 48:35.496
Geez, I told them I was fine.

48:40.084 --> 48:44.255
Gosh, those sudden outbursts
must be what's keeping him so feisty.

48:44.338 --> 48:45.548
[box clatters]

48:48.551 --> 48:50.928
-Mr. Park!
-Oh, no! Mr. Park!

48:51.011 --> 48:53.597
Mr. Park! Oh heavens, what do we do?

48:53.681 --> 48:55.558
Goodness, Mr. Park.

48:55.641 --> 48:57.143
I'll administer CPR.

48:57.977 --> 48:59.437
-Please measure the time.
-Oh, no.

48:59.520 --> 49:00.521
Right.

49:06.110 --> 49:08.696
Yes, this is Pyeondongdo.

49:09.655 --> 49:11.323
The chopper will be arriving soon.

49:12.408 --> 49:14.827
Goodness, Mr. Park.

49:23.294 --> 49:24.503
[helicopter whirring]

49:29.800 --> 49:31.844
MEDICAL HELICOPTER

49:49.236 --> 49:52.072
The patient is a 65-year-old man.
He came in about 30 minutes ago,

49:52.156 --> 49:54.783
thinking it was indigestion,
complaining of chest pain.

49:54.867 --> 49:58.662
I administered NTG. He refused to visit
a hospital and collapsed within an hour.

49:58.746 --> 50:01.665
He was in a state of stupor
with no pulse, so I administered CPR.

50:01.749 --> 50:04.126
And we got ROSC within five minutes.

50:04.210 --> 50:05.794
Are you a doctor?

50:05.878 --> 50:07.588
Sorry? Oh, yes.

50:08.172 --> 50:10.424
Then come with us. Get in.

50:10.508 --> 50:12.176
-Come on.
-Go.

50:12.259 --> 50:14.553
-Go!
-We should hurry! We'll be late!

51:02.434 --> 51:04.645
ASONG HOSPITAL
STYLE
::cue()

51:09.149 --> 51:12.194
Ventricular wall motion is poor.
We'll have to do an emergency CAG.

51:12.278 --> 51:13.279
Yes, understood.

51:13.362 --> 51:14.863
CAG: CORONARY ANGIOGRAPHY

51:14.947 --> 51:17.449
RESTRICTED AREA

51:20.411 --> 51:21.870
INTENSIVE CARE UNIT

51:21.954 --> 51:23.664
-[Jiui sighs]
-[paramedic sighs]

51:23.747 --> 51:26.208
-Thank you for a job well done.
-Thank you.

51:26.292 --> 51:27.293
Take care.

51:28.127 --> 51:30.296
-Sir, just a moment.
-Yes?

51:31.338 --> 51:33.090
-What about me?
-Huh?

51:33.173 --> 51:34.258
-Huh?
-What do you mean?

51:34.341 --> 51:35.968
How do I get back?

51:36.051 --> 51:38.262
You? Why are you asking me that?

51:38.345 --> 51:40.306
I guess you could ask your health center.

51:40.848 --> 51:42.141
I'm leaving now.

51:42.224 --> 51:43.434
-Bye.
-Okay.

51:43.517 --> 51:44.977
Safe travels.

51:46.312 --> 51:49.231
Yes, situation room.
Yeopoong One has finished transferring…

51:49.315 --> 51:52.735
So we're just supposed to
find our own way back home, huh?

51:55.070 --> 51:57.281
Then why the hell
did he tell me to come? Damn it.

52:00.117 --> 52:01.535
How am I supposed to get back?

52:02.202 --> 52:06.874
[Ms. Hwang] The last ferry's already gone
for the day, so find a motel, sleep there,

52:06.957 --> 52:09.376
and take the first ferry back tomorrow.

52:09.460 --> 52:10.628
Oh, a ferry?

52:10.711 --> 52:13.047
[Ms. Hwang] Of course, a ferry.
What else would you take? A train?

52:13.130 --> 52:14.882
Never mind. Yes, I understand.

52:15.382 --> 52:16.634
[Ms. Hwang] Good work today.

52:16.717 --> 52:17.760
[hangs up]

52:19.386 --> 52:20.387
That's it?

52:22.473 --> 52:23.474
Oh, come on.

52:24.850 --> 52:25.851
[sighs]

52:28.395 --> 52:29.396
Man, I'm so exhausted.

52:31.023 --> 52:32.024
I'm starving.

52:33.651 --> 52:35.653
[♪ muffled pop music playing]

52:41.408 --> 52:42.743
[exhales deeply]

52:46.080 --> 52:48.999
Man, to think this is
my first meal in 24 hours…

52:51.335 --> 52:52.378
[sighs]

53:01.261 --> 53:03.222
[phone chimes]

53:05.891 --> 53:08.644
[chiming continues]

53:11.855 --> 53:14.274
Clap, clap, clap, welcome to hell.

53:14.358 --> 53:15.693
You won a ticket to hell!

53:15.776 --> 53:17.695
Pyeondongdo of all places?

53:17.778 --> 53:20.155
Hang on for a year,
then make a run for the mainland.

53:20.239 --> 53:22.616
If you just got here,
does that mean you have 340 days

53:22.700 --> 53:25.703
until you're allowed to transfer
to a different province? [cackles]

53:25.786 --> 53:28.330
[Jiui] "If you just got here,
does that mean you have 340 days?"

53:28.414 --> 53:29.873
Is this guy mocking me right now?

53:29.957 --> 53:32.710
It's because you were
a traitor to the nation in your past life.

53:32.793 --> 53:35.921
I was a helmsman on the turtle ship!
So why'd I get sent to an island?

53:36.004 --> 53:39.717
Come on, 340 days will go by
in the blink of an eye.

53:39.800 --> 53:42.177
The only downside is that
you don't get to go on leave. [chuckles]

53:42.261 --> 53:45.055
Man, these people are making me
lose my appetite.

53:48.016 --> 53:49.017
[sighs]

53:49.101 --> 53:51.103
[♪ muffled pop music continues playing]

53:59.945 --> 54:00.946
[groans]

54:02.322 --> 54:03.449
[grunts]

54:06.577 --> 54:09.580
I'm so tired…

54:09.663 --> 54:11.665
[♪ lullaby music playing]

54:15.711 --> 54:18.338
I should eat before I sleep.
I'm really hungry…

54:20.340 --> 54:22.259
That ramyeon is going to taste so good.

54:29.558 --> 54:32.269
-[motorcycle engine whirring]
-[cell phone ringing]

54:34.062 --> 54:35.063
[exclaims]

54:40.319 --> 54:41.320
[grunts]

54:43.655 --> 54:45.407
Hello? [groans]

54:46.074 --> 54:47.784
[Ms. Hwang]
Doctor, why aren't you here yet?

54:50.704 --> 54:51.955
I'm still at the…

54:52.039 --> 54:53.874
Why are you still on the mainland?

54:53.957 --> 54:56.001
You should've taken the first ferry back!

54:56.084 --> 55:00.339
Do you have any idea how busy it gets
at a public health center?

55:00.422 --> 55:02.424
It's because of the emergency--

55:02.508 --> 55:04.676
That was yesterday, not today!

55:04.760 --> 55:07.012
Hurry back
or you'll be reported for desertion.

55:07.095 --> 55:08.805
One warning for abandoning your post.

55:08.889 --> 55:10.015
Two warnings

55:10.098 --> 55:12.726
and you're barred
from transferring provinces.

55:12.809 --> 55:14.895
You wanna get tied down here
for three years, huh?

55:14.978 --> 55:18.941
[stammers] I'm going!
I'll get going right now.

55:19.775 --> 55:22.194
Oh, for crying out loud.
STYLE
::cue()

55:26.657 --> 55:29.576
-[seagulls squawking]
-[ship horn blares]

55:36.250 --> 55:39.461
YEOPOONG MARINE TRANSPORT

55:40.254 --> 55:41.255
[sighs]

55:42.714 --> 55:43.715
Ah.

55:50.180 --> 55:51.640
[line ringing]

55:53.809 --> 55:55.978
You told me that I could ask you for help

55:56.061 --> 55:59.815
if I was having any trouble
with something.

56:00.315 --> 56:01.900
It's about Pyeondongdo.

56:01.984 --> 56:04.736
Is there any other way to get there
that's not by ferry?

56:04.820 --> 56:07.281
I'd be okay with
a chopper or something too.

56:07.364 --> 56:10.284
[Ms. Hwang] Stop talking nonsense
and get your tail over here.

56:10.367 --> 56:12.869
And from now on,
if you're having trouble with anything,

56:12.953 --> 56:15.414
don't tell me about it
and just take care of it yourself.

56:15.497 --> 56:16.999
-I'm hanging up now!
-Hold on.

56:17.082 --> 56:18.500
-[line disconnects]
-Hello? Ms. Hwang…

56:19.918 --> 56:21.253
Are you kidding me?

56:21.336 --> 56:24.006
[announcer on PA]
The ship bound for Pyeondongdo

56:24.089 --> 56:25.507
is now departing.

56:26.675 --> 56:30.971
All remaining passengers,
please board the ship at this time.

56:39.479 --> 56:41.481
[♪ ethereal music plays]

57:28.445 --> 57:30.197
[♪ ethereal music fades]

57:30.280 --> 57:32.282
[♪ serene music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

58:04.147 --> 58:08.568
[Jiui] The three things one must avoid
encountering on an island.

58:12.906 --> 58:15.283
-Incidents…
-Please wake up.

58:15.367 --> 58:16.827
Move!

58:17.369 --> 58:18.370
[dog barks]

58:23.834 --> 58:24.835
People…

58:32.843 --> 58:34.094
All done.

58:39.474 --> 58:40.475
And…

58:47.774 --> 58:49.776
[♪ serene music continues]

59:20.766 --> 59:25.061
THE THREE THINGS ONE MUST AVOID
ENCOUNTERING ON AN ISLAND

59:25.145 --> 59:27.063
INCIDENTS,

59:27.147 --> 59:29.566
PEOPLE,

59:29.649 --> 59:32.194
AND…

59:45.290 --> 59:48.210
"SUN, PLEASE COME OUT
OF THE CLOUDS"

01:00:00.305 --> 01:00:03.225
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

01:00:03.308 --> 01:00:05.685
[Hari] I mean, why do we keep
running into each other?

01:00:05.769 --> 01:00:07.896
[Jiui] Just be on your way
and stop crossing the line.

01:00:07.979 --> 01:00:09.648
Look at me. I almost crossed the line.

01:00:09.731 --> 01:00:11.191
Hey!

01:00:13.401 --> 01:00:14.736
Do you really not remember me?

01:00:16.112 --> 01:00:18.698
[Ms. Hwang] He actually went to
the county office to file a complaint.

01:00:18.782 --> 01:00:20.784
[Jeongbae] Come over here
if you've got a death wish.

01:00:21.368 --> 01:00:23.829
[Hari] Why get the surgery
if you're going to act like this?

01:00:23.912 --> 01:00:26.373
I'm scared! Come on.

01:00:26.456 --> 01:00:28.041
Are we expecting someone?

01:00:33.547 --> 01:00:35.549
Subtitle translation by: Yoon Hyuk Park
